General Public License, version 3 (see LICENSE). The copyright notices of the
original work are kept intact. The source code of this modified version,
including every change listed below, is available at the fork's URL above.

This fork is not affiliated with or endorsed by the JellyBox developers.
"JellyBox" is used here only to identify the original work.

Summary of changes in this fork
-------------------------------

- Renamed to "Orpheus". The application/bundle ID on every platform is
  com.github.imprudentcoding.orpheus (iOS widget extension:
  com.github.imprudentcoding.orpheus.NowPlayingWidget), so Orpheus installs
  side by side with JellyBox. The Dart package name (jplayer), the Android
  Kotlin namespace and internal class names are unchanged.
- Support links point at the fork's issue tracker instead of the JellyBox
  developer's email and Discord.
- Removed the JellyBox cloud relay (the server-plugin tunnel and its
  automatic fallback), the JellyBox cloud continuity wiring and UI
  (handoff, remote control; the inert open-source stub types remain so the
  rest of the app compiles unchanged), and the CI step that pulled the
  private optional_features package.
- Removed Sentry crash reporting and Plausible analytics, including the
  opt-out setting and the "share device list with the developer" button.
- Removed the in-app store review prompt (in_app_review).
- Disabled Discord Rich Presence (it used the JellyBox Discord application).
- The update checker and the changelog read the GitHub releases of this
  fork (imprudent-coding/Orpheus), never upstream's. The hosted updatify.io
  changelog is replaced by the release notes of those GitHub releases.
- Release workflows build without upstream's signing/store secrets: store
  uploads and notarization are skipped when their secrets are missing.
